<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Griqua</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Griqua people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Griqua are a people of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> of mixed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khoekhoe">Khoikhoi</a>, European and other descent, who speak <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaans">Afrikaans</a>. Mounted and armed with guns, they moved beyond the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a>'s northern frontier in the late 18th and early 19th centuries and formed communities under the Kok and Waterboer families at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griquatown">Griquatown</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippolis">Philippolis</a>, Griqualand West and Griqualand East.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/griqua.jpg" alt="Griqua" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adam_Kok_III_-_Griqua_Captain_-_1848.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
